459
00:35:38,801 --> 00:35:49,900
This 18502B turbine-powered aircraft can cover up to a thousand acres on a typical day.

460
00:35:49,901 --> 00:35:55,120
Each load drops electronically through a five-gate steel dispenser.

461
00:35:55,121 --> 00:36:00,020
Open the gate, and a fertilizer rains a-falling.

462
00:36:00,021 --> 00:36:04,900
Long before aircraft started applying fertilizer, farmers used everything from pitchforks to

463
00:36:04,901 --> 00:36:08,600
horse-pulled manure carts.

464
00:36:08,601 --> 00:36:13,600
With the gas engine came tractors and rotary spreaders.

465
00:36:13,601 --> 00:36:19,040
Today liquid fertilizers flow through sprayers mounted on tractors, planes and irrigation

466
00:36:19,041 --> 00:36:21,820
systems.

467
00:36:21,821 --> 00:36:24,740
Liquid fertilizers have one advantage over dried.

468
00:36:24,741 --> 00:36:30,080
They can be applied more evenly, although both act the same once they're in the soil.

469
00:36:30,081 --> 00:36:35,360
Despite the advances, delivery systems haven't quite met the farmers' ultimate goal.

470
00:36:35,361 --> 00:36:39,860
the right fertilizer on the right place at the right time

471
00:36:39,861 --> 00:36:41,560
until now

472
00:36:41,561 --> 00:36:45,160
advanced soil testing techniques allow farmers to find out exactly what

473
00:36:45,161 --> 00:36:48,860
nutrients are lacking

474
00:36:48,861 --> 00:36:52,980
and companies like N-Tech Industries in Ukiah, California

475
00:36:52,981 --> 00:36:56,240
are looking at crop nutrition from a different direction

476
00:36:56,241 --> 00:36:58,740
they've developed the Green Seeker

477
00:36:58,741 --> 00:37:03,200
a tractor mounted system that tests the plant instead of the soil

478
00:37:03,201 --> 00:37:08,760
The Green Seeker system utilizes six sensors all across the boom.

479
00:37:08,761 --> 00:37:13,800
The sensors continuously take crop measurements every second.

480
00:37:14,840 --> 00:37:20,640
The sensor data is continuously analyzed to put the appropriate amount of nutrient on.

481
00:37:21,080 --> 00:37:25,160
This is done while the applicator is running through the field.

482
00:37:26,320 --> 00:37:30,160
Some parts of the field will accept more fertilizer.

483
00:37:31,020 --> 00:37:33,080
Other parts don't need any at all.

484
00:37:33,200 --> 00:37:36,700
This is what the sensor is telling the sprayer to do.

485
00:37:38,540 --> 00:37:42,800
The GreenSeeker sensors emit red and infrared light onto the crop.

486
00:37:43,720 --> 00:37:47,920
Since green plants naturally reflect infrared and absorb red light to get energy,

487
00:37:48,640 --> 00:37:52,920
the plants that reflect less red light back to the sensor are generally less vigorous.

488
00:37:54,980 --> 00:37:59,180
These measurements from each sensor are averaged

489
00:37:59,181 --> 00:38:03,840
and sent to an interface module on the back of the sprayer.

490
00:38:04,240 --> 00:38:08,560
This information is then sent to the cab, to the computer,

491
00:38:08,980 --> 00:38:13,920
that tells the sprayer the appropriate amount of nutrient to apply to the crop.

492
00:38:14,780 --> 00:38:22,000
The decision for me to install this equipment on my sprayer here was economical.

493
00:38:22,520 --> 00:38:27,760
We're able to apply what we need, where we need it, and then we're not over-fertilizing either.

494
00:38:29,180 --> 00:38:33,420
Farmers are also getting some guidance from above with global positioning satellites.

495
00:38:34,220 --> 00:38:40,420
The GPS system on this machine receives a signal from a satellite

496
00:38:40,421 --> 00:38:45,900
and actually drives this machine in a straight line without overlap.

497
00:38:46,580 --> 00:38:50,000
On the front, there's a light bar mounted there out on the hood,

498
00:38:50,001 --> 00:38:52,500
and you can watch it, and it's tied to the GPS.

499
00:38:53,120 --> 00:38:56,700
The light bar shows zero, which means I'm dead on path.

500
00:38:56,701 --> 00:39:00,960
I reach down here and tap this floor switch, and it locks it on,

501
00:39:01,300 --> 00:39:03,840
and then from there on I don't have to touch the steering wheel.

502
00:39:04,740 --> 00:39:07,680
And that red mark is showing where we've applied product.

503
00:39:08,240 --> 00:39:12,720
What that enables me to do is to see spots that I may have missed in the field

504
00:39:12,721 --> 00:39:16,060
or prevents me from causing to have an overlap.

505
00:39:17,260 --> 00:39:19,400
With the latest fertilizing techniques,

506
00:39:20,120 --> 00:39:23,320
farmers can be gentler on the land, reduce labor costs,

507
00:39:23,321 --> 00:39:25,520
and increase yields like never before.

508
00:39:26,700 --> 00:39:29,040
My great-grandpa would be amazed.

509
00:39:29,340 --> 00:39:31,080
The computers are applying it now.

510
00:39:31,300 --> 00:39:34,860
It's went from using manure left over from your feedlot

511
00:39:34,861 --> 00:39:42,360
to being able to precisionally place the exact amount you need in the exact spot you need.

512
00:39:45,080 --> 00:39:48,760
But there are still other ways to get plants the nutrients they need.

513
00:39:49,220 --> 00:39:53,560
And one of those ways has been buried in mystery for millions of years.

514
00:39:53,561 --> 00:39:59,600
A major contributor to water pollution in streams, oceans and water supplies

515
00:39:59,601 --> 00:40:04,280
is the over-application and subsequent runoff of home lawn fertilizers.

516
00:40:05,280 --> 00:40:07,460
Fertilizer will return on Modern Marvels.

517
00:40:08,060 --> 00:40:11,340
We now return to Fertilizer on Modern Marvels.

518
00:40:15,780 --> 00:40:18,860
Many experts predict that by the year 2030,

519
00:40:19,560 --> 00:40:22,320
the world's population will swell to 8 billion.

520
00:40:23,560 --> 00:40:26,640
To meet demand, food production will have to increase.

521
00:40:28,400 --> 00:40:33,380
And to make that happen, we'll need to get more nutrients to more crops than ever before.

522
00:40:34,780 --> 00:40:38,160
Dr. Mike Amaranthus is looking for help in lowly places.

523
00:40:38,800 --> 00:40:41,560
He's focusing on a key building block of all plant life.

524
00:40:42,540 --> 00:40:44,160
Mycorrhizae, or fungus root.

525
00:40:44,780 --> 00:40:45,860
It's not a fertilizer.

526
00:40:46,720 --> 00:40:51,840
Instead, it's a web of microscopic tentacles that help plant roots absorb soil nutrients.

527
00:40:53,560 --> 00:40:57,420
And it's been doing that for 450 million years,

528
00:40:57,720 --> 00:40:59,840
when plants only existed underwater,

529
00:41:00,300 --> 00:41:03,220
and the fungi sprouted on what was then barren land.

530
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:08,740
It was the fortuitous marriage of a primitive fungus

531
00:41:08,741 --> 00:41:14,500
and aquatic plants that allowed plants to leave their marine environments

532
00:41:14,501 --> 00:41:16,200
and colonize the Earth's surface.

533
00:41:16,960 --> 00:41:19,880
And this particular fungi is called mycorrhizal fungi,

534
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:23,320
so it's been fundamental to life on Earth as we know it.

535
00:41:23,560 --> 00:41:28,560
Once it made the evolutionary leap, the fungus spread across the globe.

536
00:41:28,561 --> 00:41:33,560
And everywhere it went, plants soon followed.

537
00:41:33,561 --> 00:41:38,560
Today, mycorrhizal fungi live in 95% of the Earth's undisturbed habitat.

538
00:41:38,561 --> 00:41:45,560
The habitat that fertilizes itself with recycled organic material provided by the fungus.

539
00:41:45,561 --> 00:41:49,560
The fungi work in a symbiotic relationship with the plant root.

540
00:41:49,561 --> 00:41:52,560
The fungi receive sugar from the root.

541
00:41:52,561 --> 00:41:56,340
And in exchange, they absorb and send soil nutrients back for the plant.

542
00:41:57,900 --> 00:42:02,640
When those nutrients are depleted, the fungi simply reach further into the soil for more.

543
00:42:03,940 --> 00:42:08,620
They increase the root system several hundred to several thousand times.

544
00:42:09,140 --> 00:42:15,580
So instead of having only 20% of your fertilizer utilized, you can have 90 or 100% of it utilized.

545
00:42:15,581 --> 00:42:24,760
At their facility in Grants Pass, Oregon, the crew at Mycorrhizal Applications grows the fungi for distribution in the commercial market.

546
00:42:26,680 --> 00:42:31,840
In these 1,000-pound bags surrounding us is where the process begins.

547
00:42:32,780 --> 00:42:35,520
And that process requires a living host.

548
00:42:36,240 --> 00:42:43,440
This hay-like substance are actually the roots of the crop that was used to grow the Mycorrhizal seeds.

549
00:42:43,441 --> 00:42:52,660
We collect the seeds of the mycorrhiza, and we use those seeds to produce the next generation of mycorrhizal plants.

550
00:42:53,940 --> 00:42:58,260
The seeds, or spores, are then germinated in a sugar solution.

551
00:42:59,420 --> 00:43:03,480
After they grow up, the fungi become twisted webs of hungry fibers.

552
00:43:05,800 --> 00:43:10,980
The microscopic fungi seeds are then mixed with a clay material and made into granules.

553
00:43:11,940 --> 00:43:15,660
The fungi are ready to help some depleted soil return to life.

554
00:43:16,140 --> 00:43:22,380
The reason we use mycorrhizal fungus is because the plant roots and the plants,

555
00:43:22,580 --> 00:43:27,600
when they go into the local soils around here, the soils have been usually a construction site.

556
00:43:28,200 --> 00:43:31,400
They've been devastated. There's no microorganisms.

557
00:43:31,620 --> 00:43:33,320
There's no beneficial bacteria in the soils.

558
00:43:33,980 --> 00:43:37,240
So we put it in as kind of an insurance policy. That's how we started using it.

559
00:43:37,241 --> 00:43:44,240
Mycorrhizal applications ships half a million pounds of the fungi to customers around the globe.

560
00:43:47,060 --> 00:43:52,900
Although its use is in its early stages, the effect of the mycorrhizal fungus on crop production looks promising.

561
00:43:54,780 --> 00:44:00,640
Independent research shows up to a 20% increase in corn, wheat, vegetable, and fruit yields

562
00:44:00,641 --> 00:44:03,400
when farmers combine the fungus with fertilizers.

563
00:44:03,401 --> 00:44:12,880
and as it did 460 million years ago it has the potential to help turn vast areas of barren

564
00:44:12,881 --> 00:44:20,020
desert into productive croplands it could be a match made in fertilizer heaven and as we move

565
00:44:20,021 --> 00:44:26,680
deeper into the 21st century we can be thankful for the soil nutrients that keep us alive for

566
00:44:26,681 --> 00:44:33,160
Whether it's chemical or organic, mined, minced, or manured,

567
00:44:33,161 --> 00:44:36,960
fertilizer makes it possible to feed our growing population

568
00:44:36,961 --> 00:44:39,920
on an all too finite planet.

